[Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from their Utilization | PRELIMINARY | Section 1 Biodiversity conservation - Law and legislation  2. (a)]
(a) "Conference of the Parties" means the Conference of the Parties to the
Convention;

[Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from their Utilization | PRELIMINARY | Section 1 Biodiversity conservation - Law and legislation  2. (a)]
(a) Provide for legal certainty, clarity and transparency of their domestic access
and benefit-sharing legislation or regulatory requirements;

[Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from their Utilization | PRELIMINARY | Section 1 Biodiversity conservation - Law and legislation  2. (b)]
(b)  Provide for fair and non-arbitrary rules and procedures on accessing
genetic resources;

[Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from their Utilization | PRELIMINARY | Section 1 Biodiversity conservation - Law and legislation  2. (d)]
(d) Provide for a clear and transparent written decision by a competent national
authority, in a cost-effective manner and within a reasonable period of time;

[Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from their Utilization | PRELIMINARY | Section 1 Biodiversity conservation - Law and legislation  2. (ii)]
(ii) T erms on benefit-sharing, including in relation to intellectual property
rights;

[Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from their Utilization | PRELIMINARY | Section 1 Biodiversity conservation - Law and legislation  2. (a)]
(a)  Legislative, administrative and policy measures on access and
benefit-sharing;

[Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from their Utilization | PRELIMINARY | Section 1 Biodiversity conservation - Law and legislation  2. (a)]
(a) Relevant competent authorities of indigenous and local communities, and
information as so decided;

[Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from their Utilization | PRELIMINARY | Section 1 Each Party shall designate a national focal point on access and benefit-sharing. (b)]
(b) Organization of meetings of indigenous and local communities and relevant
stakeholders;

[Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from their Utilization | PRELIMINARY | Section 1 Each Party shall designate a national focal point on access and benefit-sharing. (c)]
(c) Establishment and maintenance of a help desk for indigenous and local
communities and relevant stakeholders;

[Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from their Utilization | PRELIMINARY | Section 1 Each Party shall designate a national focal point on access and benefit-sharing. (b)]
(b) Promotion of equity and fairness in negotiations, such as training to
negotiate mutually agreed terms;

[Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from their Utilization | PRELIMINARY | Section 1 Each Party shall designate a national focal point on access and benefit-sharing. (d)]
(d) Employment of best available communication tools and Internet-based
systems for access and benefit-sharing activities;

[Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from their Utilization | PRELIMINARY | Section 1 Each Party shall designate a national focal point on access and benefit-sharing. (g)]
(g) T echnology transfer, and infrastructure and technical capacity to make such
technology transfer sustainable;

[Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from their Utilization | PRELIMINARY | Section 1 Each Party shall designate a national focal point on access and benefit-sharing. (f)]
(f) Promotion of, as appropriate, domestic, regional and international
exchanges of experience;

[Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from their Utilization | PRELIMINARY | Section 1 Each Party shall designate a national focal point on access and benefit-sharing. (a)]
(a) Make recommendations on any matters necessary for the implementation
of this Protocol;

[Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from their Utilization | PRELIMINARY | Section 1 Each Party shall designate a national focal point on access and benefit-sharing. (b)]
(b) Establish such subsidiary bodies as are deemed necessary for the
implementation of this Protocol;

[Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from their Utilization | PRELIMINARY | Section 1 Each Party shall designate a national focal point on access and benefit-sharing. (i)]
(i) Human and material resources to strengthen the capacities for the
administration and enforcement of access regulations;

[Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from their Utilization | PRELIMINARY | Section 1 Each Party shall designate a national focal point on access and benefit-sharing. (j)]
(j) Training related to genetic resources with the full participation of countries
providing genetic resources, and where possible, in such countries;

[Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from their Utilization | PRELIMINARY | Section 1 Each Party shall designate a national focal point on access and benefit-sharing. (n)]
(n) Institutional and professional relationships that can arise from an access
and benefit-sharing agreement and subsequent collaborative activities;

[Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from their Utilization | PRELIMINARY | Section 1 Each Party shall designate a national focal point on access and benefit-sharing. (f)]
(f) Special fees to be paid to trust funds supporting conservation and
sustainable use of biodiversity;
